{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1554387-some-specific-questions-about-armor-and-primals","id":1554387,"title":"Some specific questions about Armor and Primals","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Curseborne"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-10-16T06:56:50-07:00","id":1554387,"title":"Some specific questions about Armor and Primals","content":"So what's the Robust tag in the Armor section? The book doesn't explain at all as far as I could search for it.<br /> <br /> Also, what happens to the Primal clothing when they transform? And as a matter of fact any piece of clothing and gear when shapeshifting spells are used? Accursed don't have an equivalent of the Uratha innate ability to shift with their immediate gear and the Garou's Talisman Dedication rite as far as I could tell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1876-fenixpp","name":"Fenixpp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1876_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-22T17:56:02-07:00","id":1554577,"title":"","content":"Near as I can tell, &quot;Robust&quot; is likely a mistaken reference to <i>Impenetrable</i>, similar to Bombardment's nonexistent &quot;Petrified&quot; effect for ice likely being intended as <i>Immobilized</i> - the CPG Kickstarter provides a Ritual to achieve the actual flesh-to-stone effect, not a tag applied to common magical attacks (said Ritual pulls double-duty to cover foe-to-frog types of effects as well, and requires the target already be either <i>Mortally Wounded</i> or <i>Taken Out</i>).<br /> <br /> As for shapeshifting and clothing, going by the art for the (socially-inclined) Raptors and Sphinx, it appears intended to be the player's call whether you end up with a pristine fit (albeit likely soaked in gore), modesty rags, or clothed only in said gore. With the Outcasts, their Liminal Forms already have some latitude to manifest a broad variety of phenomena external to their physical bodies as an expression of the Outside they relate to, which could be interpreted to include clothing, as long as it somehow expresses the same, so the &quot;absorb your clothes&quot; option isn't off the table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3388-r0gue_rob0t","name":"r0gue_rob0t","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}